## BASICS
- Invented by James Gosling
-  Features of Java Programming are Portable, Architectural Neutral, Object-Oriented, Robust, Secure, Dynamic and Extensible, etc.
- Pointers is not a Java feature. Java provides an efficient abstraction layer for developing without using a pointer in Java.
- Java is primarily platform independent as it primarily focuses on the principle of "Compile once , run anywhere"
- There are 4 OOPS concepts in Java. Inheritance, Encapsulation, Polymorphism and Abstraction.
- JDK - Java Development toolkit
- JDK is used to compile , debug and execute java programs.
-  JAVA_HOME environment variable is used to store a path to the java installation.

